Hello,

I am running multigroup CFAs to test measurement invariance in a sample of about 2200. My data is has unequal groups (e.g.,  1000, 300, 300, 200, 200) and skewed/kurtotic dichotomous data, with many of the 21 indicators skewed/kurtotic. I was planning on using the permuteMeasEq function in semTools to evaluate chi-square, and planning to implement 500 permutations and use the maxSparse argument for reshuffling, as that is what I gleamed from Appendix A of Kite, Jorgensen, & Chen (2018).

Given the skew of my data, I am wondering:
Do I need to implement more than 500 permutations?
Are there recommendations for reshuffling data? The default is 10, but does that need to be reduced given the skew ?
Any guidance would be much appreciated.

Thank you!
Abhishek

Benjamin A. Kite, Terrence D. Jorgensen & Po-Yi Chen (2018) Random Permutation Testing Applied to Measurement Invariance Testing with Ordered-Categorical Indicators, Structural Equation Modeling: A Multidisciplinary Journal, 25:4, 573-587, DOI: 10.1080/10705511.2017.1421467

