  anova(model1_fit, model2_fit, test='scaled.shifted').

 The results are still the same as before. i.e.:

                   Df    AIC    BIC           Chisq    Chisq diff   Df diff   Pr(>Chisq)
model1 218 102021 102421 2582.4
model2 219 102024 102418 2587.3      3.6361         1         0.05654

> May you share the call to sem/cfa?

   model1_fit <- sem(model1, data = dataset, cluster = "id", estimator = "MLR")
   model2_fit <- sem(model2, data = dataset, cluster = "id", estimator = "MLR")

   anova(model1_fit, model2_fit, test='scaled.shifted')

Best,
Serena

